SG00000183527","entrez_id":["8624"],"uniprot":["O95456"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables molecular adaptor activity. Involved in chaperone-mediated protein complex assembly. Located in several cellular components, including Golgi apparatus; endoplasmic reticulum; and nucleoplasm. Part of chaperone complex. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"O95456","text":"Chaperone protein which promotes assembly of the 20S proteasome as part of a heterodimer with PSMG2. The PSMG1-PSMG2 heterodimer binds to the PSMA5 and PSMA7 proteasome subunits, promotes assembly of the proteasome alpha subunits into the heteroheptameric alpha ring and prevents alpha ring dimerization."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}